package GambitRequestProduct {
 private import ScalarValues::*;
 attribute sdkModelAuthority:String="Use the existing official opensysml Python SDK and source-bound process custody. Parse_sources strict/strict_conformance, native Model.find/Symbol.children and Model.eval own field selection and values. SDK auto-start/download disabled. CLI projection remains an independent historical reference, not the Python model parser. The pre-change six-model/61-field SDK comparison passed on pinned servicev0.10.1. Typed field equality does not establish native runtime or whole-product admission.";
 attribute compilerClosurePlan:String="One integrated prerequisite chain: audit original host-layout authority; complete Scheme semantic HostGraph and explicit physical host/unit ownership; prove PointId/FrameSpec/root/tail/multi-shot preservation for affected mixed-host edges; produce same-profile generation/native/link witnesses; then resume the three dependent Gerbil modules and whole consumers. Native job overlap and private SSI publication do not divide a single C host. Do not run another full Make attempt until a source-bound change or independently completed exact product can alter the critical path. Do not substitute a profile variant, a generated C file, a stale object or an exit-zero diagnostic for a complete module.";
 attribute compilerPhaseEvidence:String="Historical1b387add/7308a00f evidence only; no d07f67b4 consumer admission follows. Same-profile source bootstrap508.827736s and scoped native frame/tail/multi-shot controls passed. The native build-spec census declares326 targets. That historical official stdlib consumer naturally exits0 in464.354609s, reusing323 module programs and completing the remaining3. All326 declared source identities match complete module records. Its first subsequent initialization-planning attempt failed because historical native candidates overwrote complete-program hashes; that failure is retained. After separating admissions,326 views are issued and libgerbil reaches original static SCM-to-C generation before its120.019055s timeout. The source unconditionally recompiles each static unit; per-unit completion custody is the next open boundary, not another graph-planning failure. Downstream libgerbil/lang/tools and matched release/build remain separate open gates. The bounded1s GC sample occurred before fresh pending modules completed: it is not a warm/no-change baseline or whole-wall causal attribution.";
 attribute compilerBoundaryAudit:String="The existing GambitModernCCommitAdmission::compilationUnit already owns unbounded-host source refinement. Historical pre-host-unit connection~1 exposes that architectural dependency:12820 labels,205 emitted procedure sections,21867016 C bytes and configured single-host limit0. Source configure.ac explicitly defines0 as unlimited. Do not treat this as a new discovery or silently change the profile. Existing HostGraph/FrameSpec/PointId, cross-host tail transfer, roots and multi-shot obligations govern a structural replacement. Compiler-host modernization is not another scheduler setter or cleanup patch.";
 attribute moduleNativeAcceptance:String="Historical1b387add/7308a00f completes326 stdlib programs,740 static units and the four original Make consumers. Current d07f67b4 has47 scoped native checks and complete interpreted408-case cost samples; its exact runtime has independently relinked and executed Gerbil stage1-bach in139.824s. Current d07/987c59dd stdlib/libgerbil/lang/tools now naturally complete with326 programs,326 views and740 static units; see shared-slot-consumer-custody.json. No historical binary is restamped. Original GSC censoring/common failure and unqualified comparative cold cost remain explicit.";
 attribute moduleNativeMatrix:String="Historical source periods retained below; current d07f67b4 consumer custody is recorded in shared-slot-consumer-custody.json and is not whole-product acceptance.\n| Responsibility | Removed work / ambiguity | Added cost | Qualification |\n|----------------+--------------------------+------------+---------------|\n| Metadata query | Cached identity and graph queries do not import native macro phases | Credential validation and original fallback | Real reader/import negative control passed; full product open |\n| Module native jobs | Global deferred completion cannot publish a module early; safe phase jobs can overlap | Per-module requests, threads under existing five-core quota; peak unmeasured | Actual original gxc overlap and raised-false drain passed |\n| Interface publication | SSI bytes cannot stand in for completed native work | Private interface storage and final rename | Source checked; whole consumer still open |\n| Admission | Repeated byte reads share one preparation snapshot; old native timestamps do not trigger Scheme regeneration | Per-preparation stat/hash records, mutation refusal | Framework controls pass; no matched latency claim |\n| Planning admission | Old native candidate history cannot overwrite complete module hashes | Revalidate whole module witnesses and all source/dependency identities |326 admitted,0 rejected; downstream pending |\n| Static native units |736 of740 compiler invocations avoided in the observed library run; closed units survive failed parents | Per-request identity, native effect qualification, dependency hashing, output claims and immutable receipts |740 closed;4 executed;0 unfinished; library natural exit51.450285s is not a matched speedup |\n| Consumer lifetime | Complete-program lease covers library, lang and tools; original compiled caller resolves the activated entry | Scope restoration, exact source inverse and catalogue/driver binding checks | Actual lang module protocol passes; tools remains blocked |\n| Compiler identity roles | Downstream products cannot spuriously invalidate the unchanged compiler host | Native114-host/34-target classification and full effective-input equality | Original58fe43 producer retained; no old files restored or products relabeled |\n| Same-source AOT service | Repeated driver source activation can use a witnessed native object | One observed18.619132s original build plus7.685908s native protocol smoke; Adapter source is part of its production fingerprint; current contract requalification builds once in16.0774s and runs the real smoke in5.0637s; a second same-identity admission issues no new service producer | Service readiness passes; whole tools still reaches native registration limit |\n| Full release/build | No claimed whole-result saving | Latency / peak unmeasured until consumers finish | OPEN |";
 attribute moduleNativeEvidence:String="evidence/research/retained/modern-c/request-product/initializer-view.json and initializer-view-matrix.json bind actual source, native property/real-SSI controls, graph-view derivations,119-root installed planning, fixed bounds and failed histories. Native initializer projections are separately journal-witnessed and cached by semantic input bytes plus transformation contract. Unknown writers cannot issue a view. Closed prefixes survive failed parents without granting native/module completion. generation-planning.json and generation-planning-matrix.json bind the installed prefix reader/coordinator,192 native cases,102 framework checks and the unchanged producer context. catalog-target-closure.json and catalog-target-closure-matrix.json bind the actual326-target native census, exact complete-program source set, natural stdlib exit, catalogue read/activation controls and corrected historical311 interpretation. Every result retains its executionInputs; current hashes do not restamp older native checks. static-unit-evidence.json and static-unit-matrix.json retain actual per-unit requests, completions, exact reuse, header/source qualification, framework fixes and failed parents. Historical semantic-context/library-order packets retain their original source periods.";
 attribute moduleNativeRefinement:String="Existing incremental_build.qnt owns dependency readiness, task completion and failure custody. Private interface writes and job collection are not publish/reuse. Native job completion precedes interface publication; only a stable complete module witness may enable downstream reuse. The C/GC and frame representation obligations remain in their existing Lean scope, with no duplicate temporal model. Source refinement must justify parameter inheritance, distinct native outputs, stable generated inputs, drain on exceptions and original-quota accounting. A producer-role inverse permits old complete programs only because generation and argv/cwd are unchanged; every actual generated input and dependency remains hashed. Static units use the existing incremental_build.qnt start/finish/publish/reuse separation: original process-status and close precede completion, quiescent identity and header checks precede an immutable receipt, and an authenticated source-effect-qualified transport alone permits reuse. Unknown native writers and failed whole parents remain distinct. Closed generation metadata refines only dependency readiness followed by start in models/build/incremental_build.qnt, never reuse or finish. Actual native joins and stable publication remain the only completion edge. Catalogue-only metadata reads must preserve the original driver binding; actual native writes activate the original source compiler under the existing import mutex. Initialization planning must not re-admit stale native request history over complete-program ownership. Native overlap and raised-false draining are scoped implementation tests, not whole Make or peak-memory proof.";
 attribute moduleNativeOwnership:String="IMPLEMENTED current d07f67b4/987c59dd has326 independently witnessed complete programs and naturally completed official stdlib/libgerbil/lang/tools parents. Historical1b387add/7308a00f retains its own observations. This does not close whole downstream acceptance. Planning requalifies complete module programs only; historical native candidates belong to compiler-stage admission and must not overwrite a current complete module hash. Original gxc queue/quota owns native requests. SSI remains private until native joins and source/dependency checks close. Closed managed generations enable only original dependency waits and native continuation, never public SSI or module completion.";
 attribute requiredAcceptanceParts:String="ownerExitRequirement;productRequirement;releaseRequirement";
 ref part result=GambitModernCOutcomes::execution;
 ref part sourceDelivery=GambitPendingCuts::schedulerDelivery;
 attribute queryAssurance:String="The Python repository_clues and evidence_views.evaluate entries return assurance: native ASCENT inference completion; checked byte identities or partial reference coverage; caller-declared premises whose truth is not established by attestation; and native execution not established by query. Source-bound branch_evidence.progress is a separate terminal-process and contract validator. Incomplete inference raises; missing or changed inputs cannot receive a completed-view assertion. The registered recorded-cases reference validator recomputes terminal consistency from the same hashed bytes and returns scoped case counts; it does not authenticate a declaration or replay a program. Org is navigation only. No confidence score or query-success-to-runtime-admission conversion. The recorded-cases validator additionally recomputes the guarded compiler product inventory, joins the88 admitted tasks to old/new request tuples and verifies10 actual hits/78 changed inputs plus parent failure. It rejects inflated hits, false completion, frontend reuse and unknown parent custody. This is consistency verification, not process authentication.";
 attribute evidenceChain:String="Canonical machine-readable integration is evidence/research/retained/modern-c/request-product/owner-closure-acceptance.json: integration.requirements is selected from requiredAcceptanceParts by native SysML; integration.answers is recomputed by the real ASCENT engine; integration.evidenceIdentities binds repository JSON bytes. Cached ready answers cannot grant admission. Gerbil history records original stage1 failures, official BACH success163.746s, real p1/p2 map/wind/GC success and stdlib timeout573.531s. gerbil-consumer-history.json retains actual compiler/make source and unfinished phase inventory; gerbil-map-consumer.json is independently terminal-validated. compiled-release.json records32 successful compiled/exec cases; compiled-release-matrix.json carries10 quantitative rows. None certifies complete downstream construction. No matched baseline consumer exists, so timeout causality remains unresolved. evidence/scenarios/modern-c/request-product.view.json uses existing evidence_views and repository_clues Python APIs with the shared ASCENT Library. Exact candidate-tree, profile observation and selected working-source hashes are distinct. Historical committed-branch qualification remains separate. Changed reference denies the view; recorded observations never grant runtime admission. The original input bytes reconstruct exactly from the existing committed Bazel fixture plus its existing C23 goal overlay; the unrelated configuration document is not that input. gerbil-compiler-completion.json and its normalized five-row matrix bind native completion and exact-context reuse separately from whole producer success; compilerProducts is independently recomputed by the existing Python Evidence validator used by ASCENT. All original failed histories remain failed.";
 attribute nativeCompletion:String="The existing Make worker owns one complete module program: source request, actual GSC child completions, all emitted SSI/SSXI/static/native phase files, and an unchanged imported-artifact snapshot. Python publishes only after parent reaping and process-group quiescence, through the existing execution journal. A ready credential authorizes importing that same complete interface and phase cohort. Raw frontend files, a bare native output, an unfinished task or an unknown parent cannot authorize reuse. GCC-MD header identities and original invoke argv/cwd remain part of native task completion. The issuer independently requires quiescence and requires every native input to be an owned emitted module output. A failed parent remains failed even when complete child module programs survive.";
 attribute nativeReuseBoundary:String="Historical phase-only continuation admitted88 and reused10:78 generated inputs changed. Repository gerbil-generated-input-causes.json records32 clock,45 lexical-identity and1 native-debug-source mark-order witnesses. Complete managed module programs preserve those identities together; no text normalization. The earlier source adapter imported saved complete interfaces only from a dependency-closed journal-backed cohort. That historical same-context continuation admitted105, consumed58 programs and avoided170 GSC/native tasks, then failed after101.450s at std/struct/lru~1. A separate actual counter observation reached exactly20000 global slots from12196 before loading. No stdlib/downstream completion or full release/build gain follows. This is official Make incremental policy plus frozen producer/owned/dependency inputs, not arbitrary macro/eval/native-I/O clean-build equivalence. Unmanaged initialization and unresolved provider identities prohibit reuse.";
 attribute metadataPlanning:String="The real semantic producer owns rich initialization graphs; a separately witnessed pure Scheme projection preserves actual context/phase identities while contracting initializer-visible wrappers and duplicates; original order-modules consumes compact slot views. No macro phase executes for metadata-only planning. Historical58fe43 observations remain source-bound. The new runtime ABI produces context7308a00f,326 complete module programs and326 derived views; original stdlib/libgerbil/lang/tools now naturally complete. Actual compilation retains lexical/phase activation. A derived view never authorizes native/module completion; arbitrary macro/eval/native-I/O clean-build equivalence remains outside this contract.";
 attribute metadataEvidence:String="[[file:../../../evidence/research/retained/modern-c/request-product/gerbil-make-metadata-consumers.json][Official Make histories and joined module witnesses]], [[file:../../../evidence/research/retained/modern-c/request-product/gerbil-metadata-consumers-matrix.json][Measured work and unmeasured whole-product costs]], and [[file:../../../evidence/research/retained/modern-c/request-product/gerbil-metadata-planning.json][Checked source query contract]] are repository evidence. The actual p1 reader control separates a non-activating identity read from an import that raises BODY-ACTIVATED, checks std/values identity and custom-reader fallback; gerbil-make-reader-contract.json retains the default-processor heap failure and the original stderr collector assertion separately. No whole product follows. Failed parents remain failed. Raw observed Make source and its exact producer projection are retained in adjacent source evidence files.";
 attribute metadataRefinement:String="Source-role projection is explicit: the run freezes the observed full Make bytes; only the exact checked identity/timestamp/closed-generation planning query adapter is removed from the generator fingerprint. Every other byte, tool/provider, argv/cwd and generated input remains bound. The Make library target retains its own full source identity and freshness check; dependent library snapshots still invalidate. Unknown adapter edits refuse projection. This is not arbitrary macro/native-I/O hermeticity or a clean-build equivalence theorem. Existing incremental_build.qnt owns deps-ready reuse, completion custody and fault5 redundant-build histories. Source refinement must show metadata reads do not grant completion, a closed prefix selects the ordinary ready/start path rather than reuse/finish, saved metadata retains the same dependency edges, and readiness is not invalidated by borrowed older timestamps. The historical31 duplicate rebuilds expose an enabledness/refinement defect, not a new Lean schedule obligation. Lean keeps existing spatial/frame obligations; no duplicate model.";
 attribute nativeGlobalCapacity:String="Historical official stdlib continuation failed during completion-table preparation: the old module-id called import/mx, whose saved SSI activated compiled macro phases. The native global count grows12196 to exactly20000. Both baseline3d42 and candidate runtime load the exact same saved object at a deliberately saturated table and return ___IMPL_LIMIT_ERR; this is a matched boundary control, not full baseline Gerbil-history reproduction. Whole-build planning and macro activation are mixed responsibilities. A complete validated module program already supplies dependency metadata: the next replacement must let existing Make consume checked module identity/dependency edges without activating cached macro code. Actual compilation still owns phase/lexical activation. Unknown credentials or dependencies must use the original qualified path, never guessed edges. Do not raise ___GLOBALS_CAPACITY or change the profile. The metadata-consumer replacement is now source-implemented and syntax-checked; its producer/consumer identity refinement, extra-input/output checks and full downstream tests remain required. Existing QNT owns scheduling/custody histories; native source refinement owns actual Make edges and C addressability; no duplicate Lean temporal model.";
 attribute nativeCompletionMatrix:String="Historical pre-storage ABI observations only; current outcomes are in global-storage Evidence.\n\n| Scope | Actual evidence | Added cost / remaining boundary |\n|-------+-----------------+--------------------------------|\n|78 regenerated inputs |32 clocks;45 lexical IDs;1 mark order | Observed mechanisms, not exhaustive token equivalence |\n| Coherent cold module attempt |314 native completions;106 programs;105 eligible |530.989s timeout;5 modules unfinished |\n| Same-context continuation |105 admitted;58 consumed;170 native tasks avoided;0 newly executed |101.450s failed at compiled macro phase load |\n| Failure diagnosis |12196 to exactly20000 global bindings |72.366s separate native diagnostic; no heap/capacity increase |\n| Saved macro control | Cold3GSC; two later consumers each0GSC and result42 | Focused control only |\n| Framework |45 tests pass; negative controls reject inflated counts and partial/unknown completion | Not native/full product acceptance |\n| Retained storage |315 source snapshots19362273bytes;105 module records3611588bytes | File bytes only, not RSS or peak |\n| Whole consumers | stdlib failed; libgerbil/lang/tools not complete | Whole release/build and4/4 remain blocked |\n";
 attribute catalogue:String=GambitPendingCuts::schedulerDelivery.audit;
 attribute scope:String="One complete fourth Modern C runtime replacement on vendor modern-c, based on3d42cc5b. Canonical candidate d07f67b4 has current native service/wait/FIFO/continuation controls and a complete326-program/740-unit Gerbil consumer chain. Source attribution retains common numeric debt; matched-release scope remains open. Historical8f/1b/0ec results retain their own identities. No repair-line progress or fragmented commit.";
 attribute priorityWork:String="Scheme priority-update owns STRUCTURE-tagged ticket fields, R+7 private F64 words and ordinary GC-traced graph vectors. Conversion/allocation precede leases. Full unique thread/queue acquisition validates identities and capacity. Solve all keys privately, publish each once, reposition actual BTQ/TOQ, release, clear borrowed roots and retire the plan. Generated direct-call witness scanning rejects boxing, checks, polling and unknown Scheme jumps; it is not a general C proof.";
 attribute propagationCustody:String="The public Scheme base/boost payload remains IEEE, including NaN. Every managed effective-key producer maps NaN to ordered bottom -Infinity before publication. Discovery follows one owner edge per thread, yielding a prefix and at most one cycle. Frozen external queue keys supply constants; planned waiters are excluded to prevent stale self-support. Compute prefix joins then the single cycle join privately, commit each node once. No after-publication owner retry, allocation, polling or exception cut. Retired plans cannot reacquire former graph roots.";
 attribute needClosure:String="3/3; final source/commit five-gate admission pending";
 attribute status:String="FUNCTIONAL_AND_DECLARED_COST_POPULATIONS_CLOSED; architecture3/4 pending whole REV admission; independent SMP1/12; matched cold build is a separate follow-up with no acceleration claim.";
 attribute ownership:String="One existing intrusive request vector stores immutable target/thunk/completion separately from state/result; it allocates no companion service record. Both high-level interrupt and restored-thread entry use one dispatcher and one service claim. The completion mutex retains wait/target-death semantics; it supplies no mutable routing identity.";
 attribute publication:String="One shared ordered-word interface covers ticket ownership, global publication and collective stamps. Ticket reservation is not ownership: the successful polling load acquires and unlock releases. Collective sender-private payload precedes release stamp; every fast receive acquires then copies payload before reset. A reverse tree message, not the local EMPTY flag alone, closes payload reuse within a fixed admitted population. Resource construction/destruction and population change remain separate source-refinement obligations.";
 attribute continuation:String="Scheduler THREAD_RESTORE still installs the logical suffix before service; that macro does not itself execute/copy its frames. The service resume closure reparks without returning through the break handler into the old mutex retry. Arbitrary user captures retain that full suffix. Native p1/p2 checks restore it3 times after the original target ends, with GC, balanced dynamic-wind, persistent parameter update and fresh current-thread registration; no one-shot restriction.";
 attribute fifo:String="Publish a single mailbox identity under the thread lock, allocate detached message cell before acquiring mutation permit, link initialized cell under that permit, synchronize every selective cursor read/write and release before timeout conversion. Rooted cell and request fields remain covered by ordinary generated Scheme frame maps.";
 attribute cQueue:String="C producer/consumer preserves intrusive vector slot0. get-next removes source head/tail and clears claimed node next under the same processor lock before returning. The thread-queue pop already clears next. A rerouted node must own no suffix of its previous queue; no side observer or validation check substitutes for this transfer.";
 attribute costs:String="Each actually contended mutex/join/sleep wait introduces one ordinary continuation header and one self-resume closure. The removed prototype scope vector is not part of this candidate. Internal header.denv is #f like existing Thread.cont: it is a private GC-traced frame root, never a public graftable continuation. User captures retain their full denv and dynamic-wind. Other captured frame values may still retain old parameter graphs. C THREAD_PARK allocates and copies zero payload words; the function-value fallback copies a header and binds it to the current Thread denv before graft. Exact allocated bytes, retained reachability and peak RSS require measurement.";
 attribute waitControlGap:String="Source replacement covers all original wait classes without imposing one semantic rule: mutex/join/sleep preserve durable owner/end/deadline predicates and re-register the same caller suffix. CV and I/O explicitly return interrupted-wait action #t, as the original void-normalization contract already did; that is no signal or readiness credit. I/O retains its post-wake interrupt check and caller read retry. Yield and reschedule retain THREAD_SAVE because they save actual running program state. Final kind-specific native evidence and full composition remain admission obligations.";
 attribute saveCostBoundary:String="Source correction: ___THREAD_SAVE itself stores return/frame links into the already-created Thread.cont; macro-make-thread-cont allocates that header at thread initialization. ___THREAD_RESTORE consumes the frame link, also without allocating a new continuation object. They must not be counted as fresh heap captures. Actual frame copying occurs in the _kernel.scm break handler when overflow undo is unavailable or the caller frame is heap-resident, and GC continuation-roots.inc materializes/marks saved frame chains. The unresolved service/wait refinement must identify these actual copies and roots; blindly eliminating a macro invocation or adding a retained snapshot does not prove lower work or memory.";
 attribute waitRefinement:String="Allocation occurs after initial lock release and before queue-registration locks. The hidden capture header drops denv, retaining its GC-repaired caller frame. THREAD_PARK first invalidates overflow undo, sets FP to the context break, writes the same frame to break.Next and Thread.cont, and sets R0 to the break handler; no safepoint intervenes. The callback receives the current live Thread, never the terminated original physical target. Registration acquires the original resource/Thread/processor lock order and rechecks the durable predicate before enqueue. Real completion consumes physical Thread.cont through THREAD_RESTORE; it does not consume a retained user continuation. Absolute timeout objects are not recomputed after service or late reentry.";
 attribute formalDuty:String="Reuse existing wait lifecycle, sync_message_acquire, sync_atomic_round_publication, sync_slot_retained_resources and gc_sync_membership models. Existing retained-resource/membership checks add2 positive and7 expected violating bounded simulations using32 samples/60 steps/seed173. Source masks and native libc failure counts refine construction, not arbitrary C memory or queue policy. Native-reader callsite coverage is not a permit proof. No new duplicate Lean schedules.";
 attribute unresolved:String="Current d07f67b4/987c59dd naturally completes stdlib/libgerbil/lang/tools with326 complete programs,326 views and740 static units. Original408-file GSC remains312PASS/1FAIL/95UNRESOLVED; baseline331/1/76. The entire95-case follow-up is94PASS/1UNRESOLVED in each role; all19 differential cases pass. Fourteen were not started in the original timed-out cohorts, five were interrupted. The identical fxmul assertion and_num90s censor remain explicit baseline debt, never passed tests. Aggregate timing/header effects are not universally isolated. Full interpreted ABBA and compiled request costs retain regressions; whole cold Gerbil/build comparison is unmeasured and its frozen commit-gate scope awaits resolution. Historical failures stay failed. No new scheduler, CFFI, generational GC, profile, executor, heap or watchdog change is admitted.";
 attribute nativeEvidence:String="Existing35 positive native executions,6 compilations,2 old controls and1728 owner-ring actions remain exact8f7/e63 observations. New original entry GSI40816.819609s and remaining Make109.332105s pass. Old/new compiler root controls27.101632s/27.122851s pass under120s each; original Make reuses two completed variants and builds the missing third in1.113637s. Prior120s failure is not reproduced, cause unresolved. Current full GSC counters334 PASS/1 FAIL/73 UNRESOLVED refine group failure without claiming missing coverage. See product-baseline.json and root-build-control.json.";
 attribute measuredCost:String="Historical8e cohort only, not current87: same8-column native module1b0b5e5f, predecessor0921f6d9 versus runtime3a541c7d, ABBA p1, two runs/role with identical per-role arrays:16 forced GC requests/32 non-tail caller. First observed fresh source-stack frames27 to25; warm rounds4 to2; summed frame events87 to55. Actual copied words76872 to76968 (+96 across16 rounds, +6/round=48 bytes at64bit); source words+64; objects+4/round. Planned/issued copy sections remain1 each round. Observation vectors are retained equally in both roles. Not allocation, unique graph size, peak RSS or overall throughput; mature heap frames still undergo full-GC traversal.";
 attribute producerEvidence:String="Runtime e63f7d8e completed source bootstrap266.202844s, clean2.020066s, dummy0.089693s and stock core32.144213s in original600s envelope with two phase1-4 passes. Test-only8f7fd987 child reuses all canonical generated/native identities: zero source copies, zero generation/core execution. Historical7a9 source bootstrap timeout571.294s retained; never promoted to a completed producer. Same stable workspace and unchanged Bazel/configure/Make profile.";
 attribute valueMatrix:String="| Responsibility | Removed work or ambiguity | Added cost | Evidence boundary |\n|----------------+---------------------------+------------+-------------------|\n| Owner propagation | No NaN equality convergence or stale self-supported cycle; at most R solved-key publications | Complete graph acquisition and bounded graph/tree walks | Source proof plus native PBT and same-case control required |\n| Key representation | Raw public NaN no longer enters comparator key domain | Producer in-place NaN branch; no reader boxing | All managed producer audit and emitted closure witness scan |\n| Scratch | No iterative owner-effect object or persistent VM pending table | R+7 F64 words; 8(R+5) payload bytes beyond old2-word scratch at64bit | Structural count, not measured peak |\n| Historical pre-host-unit build | Test-only child avoids Scheme generation and C rebuild | Exact earlier-period canonical/artifact checks | Earlier runtime bootstrap266.203s/core32.144s; not the current host-unit producer |\n| Closed generation planning | No coordinator source import for an issued prefix; original worker still owns completion | One typed metadata read, dependency waits and all remaining native work | Installed3-payload/192-case native control; official stdlib complete, downstream open |\n| Initializer view | Planner reads198209 bytes instead of173583452 rich input bytes on119 roots | Immutable projections plus retained original graphs and witnesses |161 ordered entries;18042 global cells unchanged; not peak or disk reclamation |\n| Whole runtime | No guessed throughput, latency or peak improvement | Whole product and release evaluation still required | Architecture3/4; independent SMP1/12 |\n";
 attribute waitMembershipGap:String="Existing WaitControl registrations is a cardinality abstraction. It does not prove native BTQ container/tree consistency or composed scheduler-dequeue versus request-withdraw/wake ownership. Crash observations provide a violated remove precondition, not a reconstructed legal interleaving. Derive the producer history before adding temporal transitions; retain existing Lean frame/spatial duties without duplicate schedules.";
 attribute physicalMembershipContract:String="Direct thread-start-on now acquires the same Thread start authority as thread-start plus the destination processor lease, rejecting duplicate starts. Migration holds the Thread lease from THREAD_SAVE through destination insertion and source current-thread withdrawal, never holds two processor locks, then dispatches with the acquired source processor. The fixed10000000-iteration wait is retired. The active-SMP native-reader inventory still finds effective-priority BTQ/TOQ reposition writers without an established complete queue/key-change lease; do not declare all writers closed.";
 attribute nextRefinement:String="Do not treat pre-existing fxmul or common cold compiler costs as owner regression. Preserve successful composed407/1 property coverage separately from failed original budget contracts. Qualify the actual Gerbil consumer and matched whole release/build population through existing owned workspaces; never create another source copy or relabel local GSI observations as whole release. No fragmented REV.";
 attribute commitGates:String="| Gate | Current source-period evidence | Decision |\n|------+-------------------------------+----------|\n| Tests |d07:41 frozen cases plus6 supplementary checks; interpreted408;326 programs/326 views/740 units; all four Gerbil consumers naturally exit; matched95 cases give94PASS/1 common censor in each role | Functional source review closed with explicit common fxmul/num debt; original aggregate cohorts are not passed |\n| Learning | Owned waiter/service/FIFO replacement preserves multi-shot control; VM-owned stable global cells remove fixed-array registration denial | Atomic lookup, extra wait headers/closures and metadata/native-check costs stay visible; no universal speedup |\n| Process | Whole fourth delivery; catalogue item5 of13; architecture3/4; independent SMP1/12 | No fragmented commit or repair credit; Declared runtime costs closed with explicit regressions; exact commit admission pending |\n| Models | Strict native OpenSysML324-field binding and real ASCENT; existing QNT/Lean owners retained | Bounded source/selection descriptor is rebuilt through SDK, not cached prose |\n| Questions | Actual source/case/consumer provenance is bound; cold comparison remains unmeasured in the separate build item | User-authorized cold-build follow-up; current costs retained, no cold-build speedup claim |";
 attribute diagram:String="direction: right\nowner_plan: Full owner graph before key publication\nfrozen_union: Unique thread and queue leases\npriority_solve: Private constants / prefix join / cycle least closure\npriority_commit: At most R key publications\nretire_plan: Clear borrowed roots before work unlock\nowner_plan -> frozen_union -> priority_solve -> priority_commit -> retire_plan\n\ncaller: Logical caller / full multi-shot wind and denv\nroot: Private frame-only root / denv false\nphysical: Thread.cont + break.Next\nservice: Fresh request service activation\npark: THREAD_PARK / no payload copy\nregister: Current Thread / original lock order / durable recheck\nready: Actual owner / join end / absolute deadline\ntransient: CV or I-O interruption abort\npost: I-O postcheck / caller predicate or read retry\ncaller -> root: one capture before registration locks\nroot -> physical: same GC-repaired frame\nphysical -> service: install suffix without executing caller\nservice -> park: durable wait resumes\nroot -> park\npark -> register\nregister -> physical: still pending\nregister -> ready: completed\nready -> caller: consuming physical restore\nservice -> transient: existing CV and I-O semantics\ntransient -> post\npost -> caller\nuser: Retained full user continuation\nservice -> user: call/cc\nuser -> park: late multi-shot / current live Thread\nbaseline_control: Same C and four-way fxmul failure / no new arithmetic regression\nmeasurement: matched compiled p1/p2 body latency and native peak\ngap: OPEN downstream Gerbil / whole cold release admission\nbaseline_control -> gap: does not clear unexecuted cases\nmeasurement -> gap: no whole speedup admission\ngap -> register: historical SIGSEGV retained / current positives scoped { style.stroke-dash: 4 }\ngc: Existing FrameSpec + forwarding + break handler\nroot -> gc\nphysical -> gc\nuser -> gc\nword: Shared ordered word / ticket acquire and unlock release\nmessage: GC payload / release stamp / acquire copy / reset\nreverse: Reverse tree message / consumption before reuse\nresources: VM-owned pair / per-slot construction bits\nword -> register: queue ownership visibility\nword -> message: same atomic interface\nmessage -> gc: ordered operation payload\nmessage -> reverse\nreverse -> message: next fixed-tree payload\nresources -> reverse: retained until closed VM and sender drain { style.stroke-dash: 4 }\nslot: VM sync_constructed / partial native acquisition\nreuse: Reset message state / retain mutex and CV\ndrain: Closed VM + joined carriers / dispose acquired bits\nslot -> resources: once per physical slot\nresources -> reuse: retirement retains native handles\nreuse -> message: reverse-tree cut precedes payload reuse\nresources -> drain: no child destruction\npriority: Frozen owner graph / key change and queue lease\npriority -> register: whole graph source candidate / cyclic admission open { style.stroke-dash: 4 }\nrecord: Scheme priority-update STRUCTURE / ticket + scratch + roots\nrecord -> priority: correct tagged-object ABI\nrecord -> gc: ordinary roots / allocation before lease\nownerDebt: Historical cyclic GC counterexample\nmodelDebt: Existing QNT custody / least closure / finite key laws\nownerDebt -> priority_solve: excludes iterative convergence\nmodelDebt -> ownerDebt: temporal duty / not a native witness\ncaseLedger: Python source and terminal validators\ncaseLedger -> priority: real p1 and p2 checks\ncaseLedger -> ownerDebt: scoped passes do not close this duty\nadmission: ASCENT required-acceptance veto\nownerDebt -> admission: blocks whole result\ncaseLedger -> admission: source-bound facts\nevidence: Registered Python Evidence view / checked references\nidentity: Candidate tree + runtime artifacts + profile observation\nworking: Changed working sources / unqualified\nevidence -> identity: ASCENT shared Library\nevidence -> priority: source and scoped native facts / no whole admission\nworking -> evidence: stale reference rejects query\n\nfrontend: Unadmitted frontend / macro capability closure open\ncompilerTask: Existing gxc invoke / physical output claim\ncompletion: Successful native return / output + MD reads\nquiescence: Parent reaped / group quiescent\ncompletionJournal: Existing Evidence journal / header + runId\nreuseTask: Same argv cwd source provider headers output\nfrontend -> compilerTask\ncompilerTask -> completion\ncompletion -> quiescence\nquiescence -> completionJournal\ncompletionJournal -> reuseTask: immutable witness before derived cache\nreuseTask -> compilerTask: changed identity executes\n\nmodule_program: \"Complete module program\"\nmodule_program -> native_completion: \"Actual child return and all metadata writers\"\nmodule_program -> dependency_frontier: \"Exact imported cohort, closed under dependencies\"\ndependency_frontier -> ready_interface: \"Journal + stable bytes + quiescent parent\"\nready_interface -> downstream: \"Actual macro consumer imports same lexical cohort\"\n\nglobal_addressability: \"Native global addressability: 12196 -> 20000\"\nready_interface -> global_addressability: \"Compiled phase loading\"\nglobal_addressability -> downstream: \"Historical failure at unchanged capacity\"\n\nhistorical_identity -> global_addressability: \"Historical eager SSI identity query\" { style.stroke-dash: 4 }\nmodule_program -> metadata_graph: \"Admitted identity and dependency metadata\"\nmake_identity -> reader_identity: \"No admitted program\"\nreader_identity: Header reader / no body expansion\nreader_identity -> metadata_graph: \"Ordinary Scheme identity only\"\nmetadata_graph -> frontend: \"Needs generation: original macro discovery\"\nmetadata_graph -> downstream: \"Existing Make completion edges, without phase activation\"\n\nmetadata_query: \"Checked identity / dependency metadata\"\nmacro_activation: \"Actual compilation owns phase activation\"\nnative_module: \"Module-owned requests / original gxc quota\"\nprivate_ssi: \"Private SSI until all native jobs join\"\nmodule_witness: \"Complete outputs / stable dependencies / quiescent parent\"\nmetadata_query -> macro_activation: \"only when compilation needs it\"\nmacro_activation -> native_module\nnative_module -> private_ssi: \"drain success\"\nprivate_ssi -> module_witness\nmodule_witness -> metadata_query: \"next incremental build\"\n\ncompiler_unit: \"Physical unit plan: source and scoped native pass; whole consumers OPEN\"\ncompiler_profile: \"Original profile: unlimited single host\"\ncompiler_variant: \"Historical multiple-host flag diagnostic: no producer admission\"\ncompiler_unit -> native_module: \"source-owned plan; whole consumers still required\"\ncompiler_profile -> compiler_unit\ncompiler_variant -> compiler_unit: \"counterfactual, not acceptance\"\n";
 attribute writerCoverage:String="All managed effective-key stores, including thread creation, use one in-place F64 normalization producer. Reads remain raw non-NaN ordered keys; no boxing reader wrapper. Public setters and existing boost/unboost/inherit macros share full owner-plan acquisition. Private raw/FFI/serialization field mutation is outside this adapter and grants no arbitrary-writer admission. Existing automatic insertion/unlock inheritance hooks remain disabled; this solves the owner closure reached by the existing key-update triggers.";
 attribute retainedSyncLifecycle:String="sync_constructed is a VM control array indexed by the existing processor bound, not a new PSTATE field or identity table. Bit0 acquires mutex, bit1 acquires condvar; a failed native constructor never publishes a member. Setup owns interrupt failure unwind. Processor cleanup destroys neither resource; reset occurs after old-set rendezvous and retired receiver join, with uncertain launches refusing reuse. Old signal tails may touch the retained pair but cannot overwrite the new payload after the reverse-tree cut. Closed VM/member entry and joined known carriers precede disposal; POSIX destroy success clears each bit, refusal retains control for retry. Unpublished unexpected teardown failure retains the constructor control and must not authorize caller free or blind setup retry.";
 attribute closureProof:String="Let k(x)=bottom for NaN and x otherwise. Ordered extended real keys modulo signed zero form a max-semilattice. With frozen graph leases, c_i=k(boosted_i) join maximum external waiter key. Every planned waiter is an internal edge, not a constant. Along prefix e_i=c_i join e_(i-1). The cycle value M joins all cycle constants and incoming prefix. These assignments satisfy every owner equation; any fixed point dominates each constant and incoming value, hence dominates M. At most R publications follow private solve. Structural traversal terminates under existing valid finite owner/BTQ invariants; not a wall-clock latency bound.";
 attribute gcBoundary:String="The mutation lease is deliberately nonpolling through partial red-black edits. GC waits for a finite, source-bounded operation, then existing safepoints resume participation; this is not mid-edit preemption or wait-freedom. All retries, allocation and classification precede shared writes. In-place F64 producer normalization avoids the boxing/checks observed in rejected return-value and let-temporary prototypes. Emission witness scan is source-bound and not a complete C verifier.";
 attribute failureCustody:String="Before publication a refused lease or exception leaves the old shared keys intact and releases borrowed roots. After the first shared key store no supported Scheme interruption/exception is admitted until fixed-count completion and release. A retired workspace cannot replay stale keys. Arbitrary OS worker death or corrupt/private field mutation inside the lease is outside this proof; no unknown physical write is relabeled safe.";
 attribute productAttribution:String="Current paired95-case follow-up preserves the same source bytes, SDK roles and300/90s bounds:94 pass and only_num remains censored in both roles. Original19 differential cases include14 unstarted and5 interrupted at parent deadlines; all now pass in each role. Original baseline and candidate fxmul failure signatures are independently identical. The public baseline role projection corrects a workbench-producer label using actual baseline SDK artifacts/argv. Prior0ec and currentd07 share GSI/GSC bytes and all26 RTS archive member bytes; archive metadata differs, and target-header equivalence or whole timing causality is not inferred. No numeric fix or compiler optimization is added here.";
 attribute releaseMeasurement:String="Current d07f67b4 retains full408-case interpreted ABBA, original e52-fixture8-build/16-execution data in shared-slot-cost.json, and a separately qualified argument-only fixture98971f5c in argument-only-inputs.json and argument-only-cost.json. The fresh two ABBA cycles have8 builds and16 natural executions: p1 median0.006810665s baseline versus0.009161115s candidate (+34.51%); p2 median0.018803120s versus0.024389982s (+29.71%). All4096 requests,8192 multi-shot resumes,4096 identity messages and16 explicit GC operations remain. Per-execution latency distributions and native peak/RSS are retained; these regressions must be dispositioned, never selected away. Whole matched cold build and aggregate peak remain unmeasured. The mixed SDK static archive is not baseline static-link evidence; the actual dynamic path has no archive operand.";
 attribute compiledCoverage:String="Historical1b77-case deficit retains its original period. Current d07f67b4 full original408 GSC:312PASS/1FAIL/95UNRESOLVED, versus same-profile baseline331/1/76. There are19 baseline-pass/current-unresolved cases. Earlier0ec has identical GSI/GSC executable bytes and364/1/43; executable identity does not equate all header-dependent compiled modules or explain timing variation. All original77 cases passed in that earlier source period, but the final19 remain open. No subset or started filename replaces the failed whole300/90-second cohort. See shared-slot-coverage.json.";
 part def Adapter { ref part need:GambitModernCOutcomes::Need; attribute path:String; attribute contract:String; attribute status:String; }
