  part nativeConstruction:CompilerPhaseBoundary {
   ref part :>> runtimeConsumer=product;
   attribute staticUnitCustody:String="The original libgerbil work group produces370 Scheme-to-C and370 C-to-object units. A typed nine-field request identifies context, role, program, argv, cwd, source, source blob, output and contract. Existing process-status and close establish result custody; immutable completion plus stable source/header identities establish reuse. Batch failure retains independently closed units but cannot issue parent completion. Existing incremental_build.qnt start/finish/publish/reuse owns the temporal distinction; no new Lean temporal obligation is introduced.";
   attribute compilerServiceReadiness:String="The same driver source may become one original gxc-produced native service. Input stability, output alias exclusion, quiescent original producer, immutable journal custody and a real native module/protocol smoke are all required before publishing its ready transport. Source loading remains the bootstrap path. Host-role and downstream-role classification must precede effective input equality; observing target-output changes does not authorize relabeling products. Both gxc and child GSC must use the existing p1 profile because original run.sh replaces GAMBOPT. Readiness and whole downstream admission are separate.";
